★ Caught only by a reviewer whose OWN runs disagreed: p1/K2
  Those cells are marked *. The candidate found it in one run and missed
  it in another, on the same checkout and the same prompt, so this is
  coverage on a coin flip. Run more runs before you staff around it:
  a cell that flips is what variance looks like, and at two runs it is
  indistinguishable from a lineage that genuinely covers what the rest
  of the panel misses.

